Description: Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone, known as Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone in most countries, is a 2001 fantasy film directed by Chris Columbus and written by Steve Kloves, based on the 1997 novel by J.K. Rowling.
 The film stars Daniel Radcliffe as Harry Potter, Rupert Grint as Ron Weasley, and Emma Watson as Hermione Granger.
 It follows Harry's first year at Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry, where he discovers he is a famous wizard and begins his formal wizarding education.
 The story centers on Harry learning of his magical heritage on his eleventh birthday after receiving an acceptance letter to Hogwarts, and his subsequent journey to uncover the mystery behind the Philosopher's Stone, which can grant immortality.
